    <!-- ======================================================
         ROTATING CHAOS
         ====================================================== -->

    <section class="project-case project-case-dark">


      <div class="project-case-head">

        <span class="project-number">
          01
        </span>


        <div>

          <p class="project-kicker">
            GAMING ◆ COMMUNITY ◆ CUSTOM BUILD
          </p>

          <h2>

            ROTATING

            <span>
              CHAOS.
            </span>

          </h2>

        </div>

      </div>




      <div class="project-story-grid">


        <div class="project-story-copy">


          <h3>
            WHAT IS IT?
          </h3>

          <p>

            Rotating Chaos is a Neverwinter gaming guild
            built around community, teamwork,
            dungeon content and an impressive ability
            to turn organised gameplay into complete chaos.

          </p>


          <h3>
            THE BRIEF
          </h3>

          <p>

            Build a guild website that feels like the people
            actually using it.

            It needed to house class builds,
            dungeon mechanics,
            guild information,
            events and community content
            without becoming one enormous wall of gaming information.

          </p>


          <h3>
            THE CHALLENGE
          </h3>

          <p>

            There is a lot of information.

            A lot.

            The site needed enough fantasy personality
            to belong in Neverwinter,
            while still making it ridiculously easy
            for members to find the guide or mechanic
            they came looking for.

          </p>


          <h3>
            THE APPROACH
          </h3>

          <p>

            A dark fantasy identity,
            strong gold and cream contrast,
            custom visual assets,
            clear navigation and reusable layouts
            for builds and dungeon mechanics.

            The visual design creates atmosphere.
            The structure stops the atmosphere becoming a bloody maze.

          </p>


          <h3>
            WHAT IT NEEDED TO DO
          </h3>

          <p>

            Feel unmistakably Rotating Chaos,
            support a growing library of useful content
            and remain easy enough for guild members
            to actually use mid-game.

          </p>


          <div class="project-tags">

            <span>GAMING</span>
            <span>COMMUNITY</span>
            <span>CONTENT HEAVY</span>
            <span>CUSTOM DESIGN</span>

          </div>

        </div>




        <div class="project-case-visual project-large-visual">

          <img
            src="images/rotating-chaos.png"
            alt="Rotating Chaos Neverwinter guild website"
          >

        </div>


      </div>


    </section>




    <!-- ======================================================
         HOLDAWAY FINANCIAL SERVICES
         ====================================================== -->

    <section class="project-case project-case-light">


      <div class="project-case-head">

        <span class="project-number">
          02
        </span>


        <div>

          <p class="project-kicker">
            FINANCIAL SERVICES ◆ WEBSITE RESCUE ◆ REDESIGN
          </p>

          <h2>

            HOLDAWAY

            <span>
              FINANCIAL SERVICES.
            </span>

          </h2>

        </div>

      </div>




      <div class="project-story-grid project-story-grid-reverse">


        <div class="project-story-copy">


          <h3>
            WHAT IS IT?
          </h3>

          <p>

            Holdaway Financial Services is a financial planning business
            helping clients understand their options
            and make informed decisions about their finances.

          </p>


          <h3>
            THE BRIEF
          </h3>

          <p>

            The technical version?

            Redesign the existing website
            so it better reflects the quality,
            credibility and personality of the business.

          </p>


          <p class="project-translation">

            The less technical version:
            “Please sort this website out.” 😂

          </p>


          <h3>
            THE PROBLEM
          </h3>

          <p>

            The existing site did its basic job,
            but visually it felt dated,
            generic and much more corporate
            than the business itself.

            The expertise was there.

            The website simply wasn't representing it particularly well.

          </p>


          <h3>
            THE APPROACH
          </h3>

          <p>

            Keep the credibility financial services needs,
            without making visitors feel like
            they've accidentally wandered into a bank's annual report.

            The rebuild introduced clearer structure,
            stronger typography,
            cleaner content hierarchy
            and a warmer, more modern visual identity.

          </p>


          <h3>
            WHAT IT NEEDED TO DO
          </h3>

          <p>

            Look established and trustworthy,
            make financial information easier to navigate
            and feel considerably more like
            the actual people behind the business.

          </p>


          <div class="project-tags">

            <span>WEBSITE RESCUE</span>
            <span>FINANCIAL SERVICES</span>
            <span>REDESIGN</span>
            <span>STRUCTURE</span>

          </div>

        </div>




        <div class="holdaway-comparison">


          <div class="comparison-heading">

            <span>
              BEFORE
            </span>

            <strong>
              → 
            </strong>

            <span>
              AFTER
            </span>

          </div>




          <div class="comparison-grid">


            <figure class="comparison-card comparison-before">

              <div class="comparison-label">
                BEFORE
              </div>

              <img
                src="images/holdaway-before.png"
                alt="Holdaway Financial Services website before redesign"
              >

              <figcaption>
                The existing website before the No Beige rescue mission.
              </figcaption>

            </figure>




            <figure class="comparison-card comparison-after">

              <div class="comparison-label">
                AFTER
              </div>

              <img
                src="images/holdaway-financial-services.png"
                alt="Holdaway Financial Services website after redesign"
              >

              <figcaption>
                Same business. Same expertise. Much better clothes.
              </figcaption>

            </figure>


          </div>


        </div>


      </div>


    </section>




    <!-- ======================================================
         FLAMINGO RISE
         ====================================================== -->

    <section class="project-case project-case-pink">


      <div class="project-case-head">

        <span class="project-number">
          03
        </span>


        <div>

          <p class="project-kicker">
            PERSONAL BRAND ◆ STORYTELLING ◆ COACHING
          </p>

          <h2>

            FLAMINGO

            <span>
              RISE.
            </span>

          </h2>

        </div>

      </div>




      <div class="project-story-grid">


        <div class="project-story-copy">


          <h3>
            WHAT IS IT?
          </h3>

          <p>

            Flamingo Rise is a personal,
            emotionally-led brand centred around growth,
            lived experience,
            encouragement and connection.

          </p>


          <h3>
            THE BRIEF
          </h3>

          <p>

            Create something warm,
            approachable and personal.

            The site couldn't feel like
            a generic coaching template
            with a stock photograph of somebody
            staring thoughtfully at a mountain.

          </p>


          <h3>
            THE CHALLENGE
          </h3>

          <p>

            Personal brands need personality,
            but they also need enough structure
            to stop the website becoming a diary.

            The story needed room to breathe
            while still guiding visitors
            towards the important information.

          </p>


          <h3>
            THE APPROACH
          </h3>

          <p>

            Softer colours,
            warmer typography,
            personal storytelling
            and more emotional visual pacing.

            Completely different from Rotating Chaos
            because it should be.

          </p>


          <h3>
            WHAT IT NEEDED TO DO
          </h3>

          <p>

            Create trust,
            make the person behind the brand visible
            and give the business an online identity
            that feels genuinely personal.

          </p>


          <div class="project-tags">

            <span>PERSONAL BRAND</span>
            <span>STORYTELLING</span>
            <span>COACHING</span>
            <span>SOFTER DESIGN</span>

          </div>

        </div>




        <div class="project-case-visual project-large-visual">

          <img
            src="images/flamingo-rise.png"
            alt="Flamingo Rise personal brand website"
          >

        </div>


      </div>


    </section>




    <!-- ======================================================
         VETERANS BACKBONE
         ====================================================== -->

    <section class="project-case project-case-teal">


      <div class="project-case-head">

        <span class="project-number">
          04
        </span>


        <div>

          <p class="project-kicker">
            VETERANS SUPPORT ◆ INFORMATION ◆ ORGANISATION
          </p>

          <h2>

            VETERANS

            <span>
              BACKBONE.
            </span>

          </h2>

        </div>

      </div>




      <div class="project-story-grid project-story-grid-reverse">


        <div class="project-story-copy">


          <h3>
            WHAT IS IT?
          </h3>

          <p>

            Veterans Backbone is a support organisation
            designed around helping veterans
            find practical support,
            understand what is available
            and reach the right people.

          </p>


          <h3>
            THE BRIEF
          </h3>

          <p>

            Build a support website
            that feels human and direct
            without looking like another
            institutional charity website.

          </p>


          <h3>
            THE CHALLENGE
          </h3>

          <p>

            Support websites can contain
            a huge amount of information.

            The site needed to make that information accessible
            without overwhelming someone
            who may already be looking for help
            in difficult circumstances.

          </p>


          <h3>
            THE APPROACH
          </h3>

          <p>

            Clear navigation,
            strong information hierarchy,
            plain language
            and a distinctive visual identity.

            Serious where it needs to be.
            Human everywhere else.

          </p>


          <h3>
            WHAT IT NEEDED TO DO
          </h3>

          <p>

            Help people find information quickly,
            explain what the organisation actually does
            and create trust
            without becoming cold,
            clinical or unnecessarily formal.

          </p>


          <div class="project-tags">

            <span>SUPPORT</span>
            <span>ACCESSIBILITY</span>
            <span>STRUCTURE</span>
            <span>INFORMATION</span>

          </div>

        </div>




        <div class="project-case-visual project-large-visual">

          <img
            src="images/veterans-backbone.png"
            alt="Veterans Backbone support organisation website"
          >

        </div>


      </div>


    </section>




